WEBVTT

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:04.730
Chairman Rame,

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.410
St. Pierre’s owner,
Monsieur Kirisaki, is here to see you.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.690
Show him in.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.950
How nice of you to visit, Monsieur Kirisaki.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.120
My being able to attain the post of chairman

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.920
is thanks to the recommendation of such a close friend of the King of Monaco as yourself.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.710
Cut the stupid formalities.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.250
I’ll get straight to the point.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.960
Crush the Japanese representatives.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.180
Huh?

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.260
It’s not like I’m telling you to make my
team, the American representatives, win.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.470
So, it should be a simple matter, right?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.980
Y-Yes, but...

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.860
I know that you people want
the local favorite, France, to win.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.530
If you were to crush Japan,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.150
and it were to come down to a
final between America and France,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.480
we would forfeit.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:52.740
Huh?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.170
Of course, we will be sure to
compensate you generously for your trouble.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.660
What do you think?

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.200
It’s not a bad deal, is it?

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.450
Yes, in that case...

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.210
But, I don’t really understand it.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.260
Why would you, a Japanese person...?

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.550
Don’t pry into that which doesn’t concern you.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.100
What you need is the money, right?

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.390
In that case, just obey me quietly.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.980
Th... That’s true.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.230
Oh well, I guess I can tell you.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:24.980
The reason why I want to crush Japan is...

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.190
because I HATE <i>Japan</i>.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.330
I really don’t understand that man.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.740
I was surprised when the Japanese enterprise St. Pierre

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.080
attained the rights to the American team...

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.000
And now he wants to crush
the Japanese representatives...?

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.460
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.340
but Japan´s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.630
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.950
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:03.270
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.990
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.530
Survival!!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.460
Bakers on an uninhabited island!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.870
I’m bored.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.500
The match is in three days and
we have nothing to do until then.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.750
Fool.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.090
If you wish to win at all,

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.470
then you should train yourself while you have the time.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.140
Especially baldies like you.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.930
What does being bald have to do with it?!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:04.890
Wait, I’m not bald!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.310
And when you take your bandanna off, your hairline’s receding quite a bit, too, you know...

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.390
So, you can’t really talk.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.650
Why you...!

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.190
Hey guys! I have news!

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.950
Get ready to travel.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.910
Travel? Where to?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.950
Well, I was almost on my way to heaven, wasn’t I...?

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.410
To a deserted island.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.960
A deserted island?

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.430
I wonder why all our opponents
seem really strong just before a match...

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.480
And what’s that thing they’re carrying?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.480
Attention all representatives and concerned people.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.480
You’re on board a personal plane of
the Monaco Cup Management Board.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.400
Your pilot... is me, Pierrot.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.110
You were piloting the plane?

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.110
Wait, is it really all right with you piloting the plane?

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.250
I’m carefully reading the
manual and doing it, so it’s all right.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.960
You moron!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.250
Don’t pilot the plane while reading it!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.010
This flight is going to take you to the site of the match,

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:24.090
a deserted island off the
French-Polynesian island cluster.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.970
Very well, I will now explain the
rules for the second match of the finals.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:28.890
Wait just a moment.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.600
And we have a wait-just-a-moment call!

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.930
Are we going to have an unexpected twist?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.930
I doubt the young viewers will pick up on this gag.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:38.480
Why do we suddenly have to have
the match at this deserted island?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.110
Shouldn’t you be explaining that to us?

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.740
That’s true, but...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.360
even I don’t know why it turned out this way.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.820
But, if you don’t understand,
there’s no way we possibly could!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.700
I’m sorry.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.630
But, there are things even a clown doesn’t know!

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:56.880
That again?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.170
It’s just that this morning, there
was a sudden call from the chairman.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.380
And things suddenly turned out this way.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.880
Don’t steer with your feet!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.340
How unsightly, Japanese representative.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.390
The word of the Management Board is absolute.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.890
If you don’t like it, then it’s best that you forfeit.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.600
Oh, the dude at the highest level isn’t here.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.860
Anyway and either way, I’m going to
explain the rules for the second match.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.360
First, look at this map.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.080
This is Tahitin Island.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:38.720
Once we reach the island, we’d like for
each team to go to their specified location.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.420
Wait a moment!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.380
Why is the Japanese team alone so isolated?

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.630
I don’t know that either.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.630
In other words, you don’t
really know anything, do you?

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:55.850
But... the chairman said that being
isolated was not necessarily a disadvantage.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.850
Apparently you can catch more fish
there, so there are advantages too.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.780
You have to live on this deserted island for a week.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:07.360
So, you have to acquire food by yourselves as well.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.870
One week?!

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.860
The top four teams to make

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:15.120
a delicious bread in that one week will pass.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:19.790
The topic is to make a sweet and delicious bread.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.790
Since you can get salt easily from the sea,

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.630
salty breads will not be accepted.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:30.800
As for the ingredients, the only
thing you’ll get from us is the flour.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.890
All other ingredients, including the
yeast, must be collected from the island.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.350
What was that?!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.860
Yay! Yay!

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.360
All right. What do we do?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.700
Flour... and a flare to signal when we’re finished...

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.570
And that’s it.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.200
What are we supposed to do?!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.660
To do...

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.080
To do... To do...

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.580
Hey, Suwabara, let’s work
together as friends for this round.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.300
Since we’re both bald!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:10.930
Whoa, it’s a tunnel!

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.230
I’m not bald!!
Whoa, it’s a tunnel!

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.020
I’m not bald!!

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.390
Oh, very well.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.360
Because if we don’t seriously
cooperate this time, we may not survive.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.150
So, what should we do now?

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:36.740
The topic is to make a sweet and
delicious sweetened bread in a week.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.870
We can make the yeast by mixing flour and water.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.750
So, let’s leave that aside.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.930
The trouble is going to be
getting water and the sugar we need.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.420
I think that we should get away from here

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.300
and head to the center of
the island as soon as possible.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.300
Yeah.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.550
While it may be a deserted
island, this is a southern island,

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:57.310
so once we get to the center, we
should be able to find fruit or something.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.890
As long as we have fruit,
we can make something like jam.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.180
All right.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.600
We’ll swim around to the other side of
the island first thing tomorrow morning.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.360
Okay?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.150
Yep!

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.010
I don’t really think we can take our time with this.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:10.940
Why not?

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.610
Why not, you ask?!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.460
Because we already have water lapping at our feet.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.160
The flour will get wet!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.540
This is probably a beach which disappears at high tide.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.250
Leave the luggage to me!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.300
Swim, Azuma! Kawachi!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.210
Okay!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:29.920
Yep!

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.590
Serving champagne here!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:35.680
Here!

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.270
Here!

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.850
Here!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.650
Oh, thank you.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:47.150
But, I kinda feel bad about this.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:51.150
I mean, Kazuma and the gang are having a
hard time on the deserted island after all...

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.400
Yeah. I guess I’ll take a look before the sun sets.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.910
Oh no!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.540
The beach is not there!

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.410
What?!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.410
You’re right!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.410
Hey, Mr. Pierrot!

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.840
Did you need something of me?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.960
The beach that was supposed to be the
main base for the Japanese representatives...

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:13.920
is under the sea!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.680
Pierrot Eye!

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.720
Oh, you’re right!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.940
Aiyee...

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:27.640
How can he see without even using binoculars?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.360
Either way, please send out a search party immediately!

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.650
I’m worried about them.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.190
I can’t do that.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.650
What? Why not?

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.240
There are things that even a clown can’t do.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:41.700
Because, if I were to lend them a
hand, they’d be automatically disqualified.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.410
What are you saying?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.700
If they die, it won’t matter
whether or not they’re disqualified!

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.420
It’s all right. They’re alive.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.010
Once you’re a world-level clown,

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.880
you have a heart sensitive enough to know

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:01.140
whether or not everybody in your
audience of 10,000 has made it home safely.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.810
And I feel that they’re still alive.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.890
So, it’s all right.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.390
I wonder if this guy is really all right.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.860
It’s just as he says.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.610
Ryou!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.190
I can feel it, too.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.150
No matter what the conditions may be,

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.790
they will not die before making a delicious bread.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:24.120
Because that’s a “true baker.”

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.540
Never heard that one before...

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.620
In that case, I never really
want to become a “true baker.”

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.090
But, it’s strange.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:38.630
Chairman Rame told me that there
are advantages to Japan’s position...

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.180
Japanese representatives...

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:46.640
it looks like the chairman might really hate you...

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.190
Come quickly everyone.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.150
Wait, Kawachi.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:56.070
You’re swimming like the old soldiers used to!

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.650
How can you possibly know how to swim like that?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.490
While training for the Solar Gauntlets,

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.790
Tsukino made me swim to the point of death.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.630
I’m an expert at this now.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.080
Kawachi!

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.550
Oh no! A whirlpool?

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:18.340
Kawachi!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.050
Huh? Huh?!

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.550
That must be causing it!

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.300
Kawachi!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.310
Stop, Azuma!

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:28.220
Don’t come!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.810
You’ll get caught in it, too!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.940
Suwabara! Stop Azuma please!

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.440
I should be able to get out somehow by myself.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.530
Suwabara! Stop Azuma please!

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.280
Stop, Azuma!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.670
I said no!

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.990
Azuma!

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:01.510
Let go.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.470
Let go of me, will ya!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.350
I have to go save Azuma!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.010
Let go.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.010
It’s impossible.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.600
You no longer have the stamina left to do that.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.270
You’d be committing suicide.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.980
You idiot!

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.480
Azuma’s not dead!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.780
This is all your fault!

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:20.740
Why didn’t you stop Azuma?

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.410
I couldn’t catch up.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:29.910
No, even if I had caught up, the
chances of Azuma struggling were high.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.250
In that case,

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.540
I wouldn’t have stopped Azuma.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.500
Because, we can’t allow the
flour to get wet at any cost!

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:54.320
You no longer even had the
strength to throw a proper punch.

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.000
Please be alive, Azuma.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:09.960
Azuma... where are you?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.240
Azuma!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.200
Stop it already.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.670
What are you doing?!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:20.130
How long do you plan on moping?

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.710
Crying is not going to bring Azuma back.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.300
I don’t need you telling me something like that.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:26.470
You cold-hearted beast.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.100
At that time...

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:33.650
If you had saved Azuma
instead of worrying about the flour...

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:37.940
How long are you going to worry about stupid things?

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.610
Why don’t you just keep
crying forever then?

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:41.730
I’m going.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:46.950
If we don’t have anything
ready for when Azuma comes back,

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.990
then we’ll have truly failed him.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.700
And, can you not hear it?

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:55.040
While it may have been for a brief moment,

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.750
we faced death together as companions.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.750
Can you not hear your friend’s voice?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.600
I can hear it.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.670
I can hear the sound of
Azuma’s soul screaming out to us.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.150
Suwabara...

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.760
Kawachi...

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.010
It’s true...

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.600
Now that he says it, I get the
feeling I can hear his voice...

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.200
Kawachi...

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.190
Suwabara...

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.310
Now I understand.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.940
This is Azuma’s soul screaming out, right?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.230
Listen please, Kawachi...

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:28.030
I guess you can also hear it, huh?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:32.250
Listen up Kawachi, Azuma will be sure to come back.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.490
So, until then,

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:38.580
let’s collect as many
ingredients as possible to greet him with.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.630
You’re right.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.000
Let’s start with fruit.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.220
Yeah.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.210
W-Why?

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:47.500
You’re both so cruel.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.630
Kawachi...

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.470
Suwabara...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:55.050
How could you not notice when I was so close to you?

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.360
You’re so cold.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.030
I can’t go on anymore.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:03.650
I seem to be wounded.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.120
And I’m hungry...

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.620
Where am I?

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.290
It’s pitch-black.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.580
Oh, I see.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.750
I’m dead, aren’t I?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:25.630
But, since it’s pitch-black,
I guess I didn’t go to heaven.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.430
I don’t think I spent my days badly, but...

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.390
Looks like he’s come to.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.140
Muhammad.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.010
Cleo.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:36.940
Yes Sir!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.280
What’s this?!

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:52.910
Using the powers of Egypt’s symbol,
the pyramid, we have treated your wounds.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:53.780
Treated?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.790
Oh, it’s true.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.450
My wounds are healed.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.660
And, who are you guys?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:01.290
We are...

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.250
Sphinx Blue!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.750
Cleopatra Pink!

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:10.260
Pyramid Red!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.550
The Egyptian representatives.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.010
Let me explain.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.100
The Egyptian representatives
are the messengers of justice.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:22.020
We are here to end injustice in the Monaco Cup.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.020
Geez, what’s with this island?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.570
It’s a southern island.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:33.660
Yet however much we’ve walked, we haven’t come by a single thing that looks like fruit.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.660
Where in the world can they be?

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.160
I got it.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.250
The fruit must be there.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.290
Huh?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.500
The north. Let’s head north.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.000
North?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.290
This time, our coming to this deserted island was

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.460
decided by the Monaco Cup Management Board.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:53.710
Oh! They’re hoping for the local team, France, to win.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:54.710
In other words...

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:58.310
We can assume that trees with
fruits that can be used as ingredients

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:02.640
will be plentiful in the north, where France is stationed.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.480
Exactly.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.310
That committee is made up of

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:09.820
people who leak the rules to only
the French representatives beforehand.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:12.900
I guess it wouldn’t be strange if the French team
is being favored and supported over everybody else.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:13.990
Let’s go.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:20.910
But if that’s the case, then they must really hate us.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.960
We’re the farthest away from the
point where the ingredients are plentiful.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.000
And our location was the kind that sunk into the sea.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.580
I wonder why...

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.920
At least <i>I</i> haven’t done
anything for the committee to hate me.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.470
You stupid, bald twerp!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:38.380
What about your disgraceful behavior at the exhibition?!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:44.980
I guess the committee has no sense of humor.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:48.900
Maybe I really should
disembowel this baldy right here, but...

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:51.900
Suwabara!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:55.490
This time, all of us almost died!

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:59.020
No matter what, it’s strange
for them to go so far as this.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.950
It may be that...

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.370
hidden somewhere within the
trials we face on this deserted island

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.410
is a big conspiracy.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.170
So that’s how it is.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.510
The Japanese representatives’ location has sunk into the sea.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.550
With this, we can be certain of their defeat.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.420
Weak.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:21.430
What?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.770
What’s the big deal in losing their location?

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.940
While there may have been whirlpools there,

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:30.690
they probably survived since they were near the shore.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.940
Of course.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.440
I wasn’t really planning on killing them...

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:38.660
I mean, if we were to have deaths...

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.820
I don’t really mind if they die, you know...

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.780
Huh?

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.090
Even if they died, it would be a mere <i>accident</i>.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.000
But...

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.630
And, if it comes down to you
having to take the responsibility,

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:54.170
just quit as the chairman.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.920
We’ll give you an equivalent post at St. Pierre.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:01.420
A post such that you won’t have
to work for another day in your life.

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:02.930
Very well.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.970
Cockroaches are very persistent creatures.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.680
If you don’t intend on killing them,
you can’t get rid of them.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:13.900
I expect that next time, your
plans won’t be as weak as this.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.400
Very well.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:19.650
What a terrifying man.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.150
This is not enough for him...?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.990
It can’t be helped.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.040
I should get my next plan ready.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.580
Paradise.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:33.420
This is truly paradise, Brother.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:35.420
The sea is an emerald green.

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:37.840
The fruit is bountiful and delicious.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:38.920
A true paradise.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:44.260
It’s a pity that we have to make bread and return.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:45.890
Oh, come to think of it...

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.930
we have a gum boat and oars in our mantle.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.810
Let’s get them out later?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.520
Cut it out, Edward.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.440
We haven’t come here to play–

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.820
French representatives...

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.650
Are things going well there?

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.820
Why if it isn’t Chairman Rame!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.950
I’m embarrassed to say that
we’re rather enjoying ourselves.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.450
Actually, I have a request.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.950
What?!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:17.630
He wants us to set fire to the
forest after we’ve gotten the fruit?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.710
What can the chairman be thinking of?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:23.300
As long as the fruit is gone,

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.050
it doesn’t matter that they’re the
best eight countries in the world.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:29.180
It’ll be impossible to make a
sweetened bread on a deserted island.

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:34.940
The chairman wishes for our victory over everyone else’s, Edward.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.360
I see.

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:40.450
The chairman is such a considerate person!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.830
A splinter got into my foot!

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.000
I can’t take this anymore!

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.540
I don’t wanna walk anymore!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.920
I <i>can’t</i> walk anymore.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:01.420
You really are a completely useless baldy.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.680
I’m not as tough a baldy as you.

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:06.800
I’m NOT BALD!

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:12.350
Oh, whatever.

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:13.850
Wait there.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:16.490
I’ll get the fruit myself.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:21.520
Kawachi, let’s go immediately.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.900
Huh? But why?

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:26.400
Didn’t you just say you’d go by yourself?

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.870
“But why,” you say?!

00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:30.990
Because we’re surrounded by a sea of fire!

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.950
What was that?!

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:09.230
It's just not possible to make sweet, tasty bread without any fruits!

00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:13.430
Every day, every day, we are...

00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:14.930
I'm really not liking this!

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.600
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.990
And now you must swim!!
<i>Tai</i>-yaki-kun of the South Island!

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:23.270
When you want to make bread, but...

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.150
At times you want to make bread, but don’t have yeast:
When you want to make bread, but...

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:25.170
Knead a small amount of flour and water together.
When you want to make bread, but...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:27.070
Knead a small amount of flour and water together.

00:24:27.070 --> 00:24:29.450
This allows yeast to grow, and you
can make your very own native yeast.

00:24:29.450 --> 00:24:31.700
Go to a deserted island and test it out.

00:24:32.030 --> 00:24:33.000
Okay!
